sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch13-05> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Among closely allied wild sheep (Argali) the constant angle of the horn's logarithmic spiral is nearly the same, and the species differ chiefly in the helical shearing component.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Argali horns share a spiral angle but differ in their shearing (helical) component";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter XIII, “The Shapes of Horns, and of Teeth or Tusks: with a Note on Torsion”; topic “Helical component of horns”. Scope: Asiatic wild sheep (Ovis ammon, O. poli, O. hodgsoni)"
}
